  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for New York's 24th Congressional District pits incumbent Republican Representative Claudia Tenney against a field of Democratic and independent challengers. This district stretches along Lake Ontario from Niagara Falls to Jefferson County and is considered reliably Republican. Tenney advanced from the Republican primary unopposed after it was canceled. The Democratic primary, scheduled for June 23, 2026, features Alissa Ellman, a disabled Army veteran and former VA employee, and Diana Kastenbaum, a former manufacturing CEO. Additionally, independent candidates Todd Sloan (Upstate Party), retired SUNY Geneseo professor Tony Macula, and seventh-generation farmer Ken Estes are running in the general election, creating a multi-candidate field for the seat representing New York's 'Lake District.'",
